{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-exponential","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:q-exponential","kind":"definition","title":"$q$-Exponential (grouplike)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-laplace","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-habiro-ring"],"tags":["hopf-algebra","grouplike","q-exponential","reeb-flow"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QExponential","text":"q-exponential.md","leanSource":"q-exponential.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:q-exponential\"></a><p>A grouplike of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-shuffle Hopf algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{H}_q</code> is an element <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g \\in \\mathcal{H}_q</code> satisfying <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_q(g) = g \\otimes g</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\epsilon(g) = 1</code>. The <strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-exponential</strong> is the unique grouplike <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\exp_q \\in G(\\mathcal{H}_q)</code> satisfying the categorical flow equation</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  D_q  \\exp_q  =  \\exp_q, \\qquad \\exp_q(0) = 1.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exponential.md","heading":"Definition","number":"4.23.1","page":"b/def-q-exponential","qa":{"counts":{"pass":80,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":56},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.QExponential","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exponential.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
